// An area document is one markdown file in the areas directory, holding the
// decisions of one area of the product; needs.md holds the needs, and
// README.md is documentation, not a document of the charter. Its header
// is a title and, optionally, the code the area covers, then any prose,
// tables, lists and fenced blocks that orient the reader, unparsed and
// without section headings; then one entry per heading:
//
//	# Bucket refill
//	Code: pkg/limit, web/src/limit
//
//	## SW-118 The bucket refills from its last request at the rate
//	Status: active
//	Kind: invariant
//	Serves: STK-040
//	See: SW-063
//	Accounts: event:run.refilled
//
//	The decision, in one to six sentences, at the boundary where it shows.
//
//	Why: the reason, from the side of whoever needed it.
//
//	Scenarios:
//	1. `waited-request-passes`: a request after a wait of one token passes.
//	2. `burst-caps-tokens`: a long wait earns no more than the burst.
//
//	Guidance: how to build it, when the ruling said so; advisory.
//
//	Changes:
//	- 2026-09-28: what changed and why.
//
// The field lines follow the heading, blank lines before them allowed, and
// end at the first blank line after one; the parts of the body come in that
// order, each a paragraph opened by its label. A need has no Kind, Serves
// or Guidance. The form problems are reported under "form"; ids and
// handles are what anchors, citations and waivers name.

// Scenario is one numbered scenario of a spec: a handle a test cites, the
// sentence naming an input and an observable outcome, and who ruled it.
type Scenario struct {
	Handle, Text string
	// Line is the scenario's line in its document.
	Line int
	// Provenance is who ruled the scenario, written in parentheses after
	// the handle; a scenario with none written is an agent's, provisional.
	Provenance Provenance `json:"provenance"`
}

// Provenance is who ruled a scenario: the owner, a named delegate, or an
// agent whose choice nobody has ruled on yet. It is written after the
// handle: `handle` (owner, #444), `handle` (delegate name, #12 R3)
// or `handle` (agent, provisional); nothing written is the last.
type Provenance struct {
	// Who is owner, delegate or agent.
	Who string `json:"who"`
	// Name is the delegate's name.
